  ⚠ Start a git repository in /srv/files-example and    
    take it over?                                       
                                                        
  Yes looks at the folder once more and makes the       
  changes listed below only if its list is unchanged.   
  Containers of these stacks already run, so deploying  
  would create duplicate containers and take their ports
  twice. qhost only warns.                              
                                                        
    folder: /srv/files-example                          
    case: files (files without a repository; a first    
    commit takes the listed files)                      
    owner: root, group: root, mode: 0755                
    the service can write it: no                        
    permissions are set: yes                            
                                                        
